27:["$","p",null,{"children":["The value is the matching rule. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"exact"}]," means the strings must be equal.\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"minimum"}]," means the worker's number must be at least what the action asks for,\nwhich is what makes ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cpu_count"}]," usable as a sizing hint. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"priority"}]," does not\nrestrict matching at all: the worker only has to advertise the key, and the\nvalue is passed to the worker as information. Despite the name, the scheduler\ndoes not currently use it to prefer one worker over another. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ignore"}]," lets an\naction request a key without requiring the worker to have it."]}]
28:["$","p",null,{"children":["A key an action requests that the scheduler does not list is a key the\nscheduler cannot match on: matching that action fails with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Unknown platform property"}],", and the usual symptom is an action that queues forever while idle\nworkers sit next to it. A worker that advertises a key the scheduler does not\nlist is rejected when it connects."]}]
